\] \[
\frac{5}{120} = \frac{5 \div 5}{120 \div 5} = \frac{1}{24}
\] \[
\frac{8}{3} = \frac{8}{3}
\] Now, multiply the simplified fractions together: \[
\frac{45}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{24} \cdot \frac{8}{3} = \frac{45 \cdot 1 \cdot 8}{4 \cdot 24 \cdot 3} = \frac{360}{288}
\] Finally, simplify \(\frac{360}{288}\) by finding the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 360 and 288, which is 72: \[
\frac{360 \div 72}{288 \div 72} = \frac{5}{4}
\] So, the simplified value is \(\frac{5}{4}\).</think> <answer> \(\frac{5}{4}\)</answer>

