 First, we need to convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to US dollars, and then convert the US dollars to Chinese yuan. Since 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars, we can find out how many US dollars the painting costs by dividing the cost in Namibian dollars by the conversion rate. Then, we convert that amount of US dollars to Chinese yuan, knowing that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. The calculation is as follows: \[
\text{Cost in US dollars} = \frac{105 \text{ Namibian dollars}}{7 \text{ Namibian dollars/US dollar}} = 15 \text{ US dollars}
\] \[
\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = 15 \text{ US dollars} \times 6 \text{ Chinese yuan/US dollar} = 90 \text{ Chinese yuan}
\] So, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \(\boxed{90}\).</think> <answer> 90</answer>

